  "name": "Example: Calculating the Inverse of an Orthogonal Matrix",
  "problem": "Find the inverse of the orthogonal matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069920/assets/0fdcc6a3e329666b00a45c05292d85ab2df6366ff38d5506233b6c15064d2149.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nTherefore, since $D$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{-1} & ={D}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
